cases.steps:
1. DELETE /api/shop-products/{listing}
2. GET /api/shops/{A}/removed-listings
3. POST /api/shops/{A}/removed-listings { listingIds: [listing] }
4. Read the item in GET /api/shops/{A}/puja/catalogue

1. Customer: POST /api/listing-price-requests { shopProductId, quantity: 1 }
2. Owner: GET /api/shops/{A}/listing-price-requests
3. Owner: POST /api/shops/{A}/listing-price-requests/{request} { pricePaise: 6000 }
4. Customer: GET /api/notifications
5. Customer: read the shop's shelf and POST /api/cart with the listing

1. GET /api/admin/puja/config
2. PATCH { edibleNeedsFssai: <opposite> }
3. POST /api/admin/puja/festivals { festivalKey: "diwali", title: "QA Diwali <run>", startsAt: now − 1 min, endsAt: now + 1 h, showOnHome: false }
4. Open /puja
5. Put the FSSAI value back and switch the collection off

1. POST /api/shops/{A}/removed-listings { listingIds: [<A's live listing>] }
2. POST { listingIds: [<B's removed listing>] }
3. POST { listingIds: [] }

1. POST /api/shops/{A}/puja/products { categoryId: <Kapur>, name: "Kapur Tablets", unit: "pack", variants: [{ label: "100 g", pricePaise: 14000, stock: 20 }] }
2. Repeat with confirmDuplicate: true
3. GET /api/admin/puja/submissions as an operator

1. Owner: press “Not available” on L's request
2. Both customers read their notifications
3. POST /api/shops/{A}/listing-price-requests/<L's request> { pricePaise: 5000 }
4. POST R with { pricePaise: 6000 }
5. POST R with { pricePaise: 0 }
6. As shop B's owner POST /api/shops/{A}/listing-price-requests/R { pricePaise: 4000 }

1. Open /admin/console/shops and read the shop's card
2. From the operator's session send POST /api/shops/<id>/approve with {classification: GREEN, waiveFssai: {reason: Owner will upload next week}}
3. Send the same with waiveDocuments instead of waiveFssai

1. Signed out, send POST /api/shops/registration-draft/documents-step
2. As the customer send POST {}
3. Send a body that is not JSON
4. Send {promise: "yes"}, then {promise: true, extra: 1}

1. POST /api/admin/dealers/D1/salespeople/G1/transfer {toDealerId: D2, reason: 'test move'}
2. As the operator, send the same call
3. Open D1's team

1. Open the request card as Admin A
2. POST /api/admin/referral-moves/REQ {action: approve, note: 'self approve'}
3. POST {action: reject, note: 'self reject'}
4. (Developer) in the database set decided_by = requested_by on a referral_move_requests row

1. Open the request as Admin B and type a decision note
2. POST /api/admin/referral-moves/REQ {action: approve, note: 'consents checked'}
3. Upload only the shop owner's letter and try again

1. POST /api/admin/dealer-schemes {code: 'FREE', name: 'Free again', category: DEALERSHIP, reason: 'dup test'}
2. POST with code '1ABC'
3. POST with reason 'ok'
4. POST with name 'ab'
5. POST {code: 'BP_COPY', name: 'BP copy', category: DEALERSHIP, cloneFromVersionId: BPV, reason: 'clone test'}

1. POST /api/smart-list/wishlists/<W>/order {"shopId": "<Z>"}
2. POST {"shopId": "abc"}
3. POST for the all-In-cart wishlist with a nearby shop
4. Send 61 order requests within a minute

1. As S's admin tap Decline on R's request
2. PATCH R2's request {"action": "decline", "note": "Not serving this area"}
3. As R and R2 read notifications and My requests
4. PATCH R's request again with {"action": "approve"}

1. As S's society OPERATOR open /society/<S> and PATCH {"action": "approve"}
2. As S's resident and as T's admin GET /api/societies/<S>/join-requests and PATCH the request
3. As the GoKesari operator open /society/<S> and approve

1. As Accountant: POST /api/finance/commission-rates {scope: DEFAULT, rateBp: 500}
2. As Accountant: POST /api/staff/accounting/periods/2026-11 {action: CLOSE}
3. As CA: POST /api/staff/accounting/journals with a balanced two-line entry
4. As CA: POST /api/staff/accounting/rates with a commission proposal
5. As Accountant: open /admin/finance

1. As Support User: PATCH /api/shops/{shopA} {description: “QA”}
2. As Support User: open /admin/support
3. As Support Manager: PATCH /api/shops/{shopA} {description: “QA”}
4. As Support Manager: PATCH /api/users/{id}/role {role: OPERATOR}

1. As Admin GET /api/approvals?status=ALL
2. As CA GET /api/approvals?status=ALL
3. As Support User GET /api/approvals
4. As CA GET /api/approvals/{admin request id}
5. As the requesting admin and as the CA GET /api/approvals/{journal request id}

1. Admin B clicks “Reject” with the comment box empty
2. Admin B POST /api/approvals/{id}/cancel
3. Admin A POST /api/approvals/{id}/decide {decision: REJECT, comment: “x”}
4. Admin A types a comment and clicks “Cancel request”
5. Admin B POST /api/approvals/{id}/decide {decision: APPROVE}

1. Admin A POST /api/users/{active user}/reinstate {reason: “QA reactivation”}
2. Admin B opens /admin/approvals and approves “Reactivate account”
3. GET /api/approvals/{id}

1. Admin A PATCH /api/users/{id}/role {role: OPERATOR}
2. Admin A opens /admin/approvals
3. Admin A POST /api/approvals/{id}/decide {decision: APPROVE}

1. PATCH /api/users/{own id}/role {role: CUSTOMER}
2. DELETE /api/users/{own id}/roles?role=ADMIN
3. PATCH /api/users/{own id}/privileges {activeRole: ADMIN, heldRoles: [ADMIN]}

1. Admin A PUT /api/admin/settings {key: rbacV2, value: {…, highValueJournalPaise: 10000000}}
2. Admin A POST /api/finance/commission-rates {scope: DEFAULT, rateBp: 450, note: “QA”}
3. Admin A POST /api/registration-fees with a new amount and reason
4. Admin A DELETE /api/admin/settings?key=rbacV2
5. Read the live values
6. Admin B approves each on /admin/approvals

1. PATCH /api/staff/support/tickets/{id} {assigneeId: gk-oplim}
2. Open /admin/support/{id} as the Support Manager and read the assignee picker
3. Assign the ticket to the customer
